  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/77e61619-9ac8-4ca3-915e-7e2c83f345b6.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 144px;\"/></p><p>Ratio of EMF developed will be given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, current in secondary circuit will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math></p><p>Hence, potential drop across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kΩ</mi></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>7</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kΩ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
